<title>USA: Fed says it adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed says it adds reserves via overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system through overnight system repurchase agreements on Tuesday, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a temporary reserve addition.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-9/16 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>(( --North  American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
